accordingly.

The chat/embedding/omni checkpoints pinned by flake.nix carry their own
terms: the Gemma-family weights (google/gemma-4-E4B-it and variants,
nvidia/Gemma-4-31B-IT-NVFP4) ship under the Google Gemma Terms of Use,
a use-restricted custom license -- review it before any deployment; the
Qwen-family weights (Qwen/Qwen3.5-*, Qwen3-Embedding, Qwen3-Omni,
Qwen3-TTS, Qwen3-ForcedAligner, unsloth/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4) ship under
Apache-2.0.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
System One decisions (rust/crates/nv-laya)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

Laya and its pretrained checkpoints are by Convai Innovations and the
Laya contributors (https://github.com/NandhaKishorM/laya, Apache-2.0);
the weights are downloaded separately and are not bundled.

rust/crates/nv-laya/tests/fixtures/upstream_parity_cases.json reproduces
the parity cases and recorded sequence lengths of laya-mlx
(https://github.com/mizorewww/laya-mlx, commit fc1df628, Apache-2.0,
copyright 2026 laya-mlx contributors). The final-head pruning and the
length-grouped padded pass in the crate follow that project's published
performance research.

----------------------------------------------------------------------
Contrastive Language Models (System One CLM)
----------------------------------------------------------------------

The CLM head architecture, typed-question schema and bidirectional contrastive
objective follow Contrastive-LM/CLM, revision
bb42c6c5bf914fd449bed2f6ca65be80602cb1f7 (Apache-2.0), by Jacky Kwok and the
CLM contributors: https://github.com/Contrastive-LM/CLM . The training scripts
import that implementation from a separately downloaded checkout. CLM-v0.1-8B
and its Qwen3-8B encoder weights are Apache-2.0 and downloaded separately.
Public training dataset sources and exact revisions accompany each run's
public/manifest.json; their licenses continue to apply to those datasets.
